--- diagnostics ---
SC0420 @48..54 `String` cannot cross the C boundary
  note a C string is NUL-terminated and a Science `String` is UTF-8 bytes with a length; write `ffi.CStr` for one that is &and `ffi.CString` for one Science owns, and expect the copy both of them make
SC0420 @73..89 `Map` cannot cross the C boundary
  note a `Map` is a Science hash table, and the C side does not know its layout
SC0420 @108..119 `Option` cannot cross the C boundary
  note an `Option` is a niche, and which niche depends on the payload; the C spelling of absence is a null `ffi.Pointer`
SC0420 @124..140 `Result` cannot cross the C boundary
  note a `Result` is a Science choice; a C function reports failure with a status the safe wrapper converts
SC0420 @157..167 a tuple cannot cross the C boundary
  note C has no tuple; declare a `type` marked `implements ffi.CLayout` and pass a pointer to it
SC0420 @186..199 `any Summarize` cannot cross the C boundary
  note a dynamically dispatched value is a Science pair of pointers, and C knows neither half
SC0421 @217..227 `Array[T]` has no C representation
  note the length does not cross the ABI — it exists on the Science side so that the wrapper's bounds check is an expression the compiler checks
  note a call site still passes the array: `&Array[T]` coerces to `ffi.Span[T]` there, and `.span()` names the conversion where it has to be written out
SC0420 @246..252 `String` cannot cross the C boundary
  note a C string is NUL-terminated and a Science `String` is UTF-8 bytes with a length; write `ffi.CStr` for one that is &and `ffi.CString` for one Science owns, and expect the copy both of them make
SC0420 @277..285 `Box` cannot cross the C boundary
  note a `Box` owns what it points at under Science's allocator; pass `ffi.Pointer[T]` and say in the binding who frees it
